    "body": "**The short answer:** for multi-step workflows you can see and branch without writing a service, our pick is **Make** (92% match on [/best/automation](https://bestbotfor.com/best/automation)). Choose **Zapier** (90%) if you want the widest app directory and the gentlest editor. Choose **n8n** (90%) if you want to self-host or drop into custom code.\n\nShort on time? [Get a pick in 30 seconds](https://bestbotfor.com/).\n\n## Verdict by use case\n\n| If your job is... | Start with | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Multi-step workflows with branches, built visually | **Make** | Scenarios are a visual map of modules, with routers for branching |\n| \"When X happens in app A, do Y in app B,\" no-code | Zapier | The widest app directory and the gentlest editor |\n| Self-hosting, data control, or custom code | n8n | Free self-hosted Community Edition; code nodes when the happy path isn't enough |\n| AI-heavy flows built with drag-and-drop | Gumloop | Built for AI automations |\n| A cheaper open-source alternative to Zapier | Activepieces | Open source, lower cost |\n| Developers mixing code and integrations | Pipedream | Code and integrations in one workflow |\n| Repetitive tasks in the browser | Bardeen | Browser-task automation |\n\n## Our pick: Make\n\n**Match for this job:** 92%. **Our rating:** 3.2, #5 of 7 in Automation. **Skill level:** intermediate.\n\n**Why the match and the rating differ:** match measures how well a tool matches the specific job of visual, branching workflows. The overall rating weighs the whole category. On overall rating, n8n (4.1, #1 of 7) and Zapier (3.7, #3 of 7) score higher than Make. Make leads on fit because the visual scenario builder matches this job directly.\n\nMake shows the workflow as a map of modules. It handles branching better than a simple two-step zap, and it asks a bit more of you up front. Make says it integrates with more than 1,000 third-party apps, and custom apps can connect any service with a public API.\n\n**Visit:** [Make](https://bestbotfor.com/go/make?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\n### Pricing\n\n**From make.com/en/pricing:**\n- \"As of August 27, credits are the billing unit in Make.\" Most actions use 1 credit. Some AI features use more. Router and error-handler modules use none.\n- The Free plan includes **1,000 credits per month**.\n- The paid plans are named **Core, Pro and Teams**, plus Enterprise. Annual payment is cheaper than monthly.\n- When credits run out, scenarios stop until you add credits. Unused credits expire at the end of the term. You can buy extra credits in bundles of 1,000 or 10,000.\n- Under 20 employees? Make advertises a Start-up Plan at 50% off Business.\n\nWe couldn't verify Make's current plan prices on its pricing page. See [make.com/pricing](https://www.make.com/en/pricing) for current Core, Pro and Teams prices.\n\n### Who should skip Make\n\n- **You want the simplest possible two-step automations.** Zapier's editor is gentler.\n- **You need to self-host or keep data on your own servers.** n8n has a free self-hosted edition.\n- **You write code and want it inside the workflow.** n8n or Pipedream fit better.\n- **Your workflows run constantly at high volume.** Every action uses credits, and scenarios stop when credits run out. Model your monthly credit use before you commit.\n- **You want the highest-rated tool overall, not the closest fit.** n8n carries our highest overall rating in Automation.\n\n## The alternatives\n\n**Zapier: 90% match.** Our rating: 3.7, #3 of 7. **Verified on [zapier.com/pricing](https://zapier.com/pricing) on October 20, 2026:** Free is $0 a month with 100 tasks; Professional starts from $19.99 a month; Team starts from $69 a month. The page shows \"starting from\" prices and we didn't capture which billing period applies, so confirm on the page. Costs rise with task volume. Choose it for the widest app directory and the easiest start. [Visit Zapier](https://bestbotfor.com/go/zapier?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\n**n8n: 90% match.** Our rating: 4.1, #1 of 7. Price label on our live page: \"Free (self-hosted); cloud from €20/mo\". Our catalog, checked against n8n's pricing page on October 17, 2026, lists Starter at €20 a month and Pro at €50 a month billed yearly, with Starter capped at 2,500 executions a month. n8n's pricing page didn't render for our checker on October 20, so those figures weren't re-checked today. Choose it for self-hosting and custom code. [Visit n8n](https://bestbotfor.com/go/n8n?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\n**Gumloop: 82% match.** Paid. Build AI automations with drag-and-drop. [Visit Gumloop](https://bestbotfor.com/go/gumloop?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\n**Activepieces: 80% match.** A cheaper, open-source alternative to Zapier. [Visit Activepieces](https://bestbotfor.com/go/activepieces?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\n**Pipedream: 78% match.** Mix code and integrations in one workflow. [Visit Pipedream](https://bestbotfor.com/go/pipedream?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\n**Bardeen: 74% match.** Automate repetitive browser tasks. [Visit Bardeen](https://bestbotfor.com/go/bardeen?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=automation)\n\nGumloop, Activepieces, Pipedream and Bardeen use the labels from our live page. They weren't re-checked on their vendors' sites for this guide.\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Is Make free?** Yes, there's a free plan with 1,000 credits a month, per make.com/en/pricing on October 20, 2026.\n\n**Make or Zapier?** Make if you want to see and branch a multi-step workflow. Zapier if you want the simplest editor and the most apps. See our [n8n vs Make comparison](https://bestbotfor.com/compare/n8n-vs-make) too. Confirm current Make pricing on make.com before you buy.\n\n**Did you test these tools?** No. Our scores are research-based, built from vendor pages, docs, leaderboards and published reviews.\n\n## What we checked\n\n- **Make:** make.com/en/pricing on October 20, 2026 (ET). We captured the FAQ (credits, the free 1,000 credits, plan names) but not the plan prices, so this guide doesn't list them.\n- **Zapier:** [zapier.com/pricing](https://zapier.com/pricing), fetched October 20, 2026.\n- **n8n:** n8n.io/pricing didn't render on October 20, 2026. The figures come from our catalog (last verified October 17, 2026).\n- **Our live ranking:** [bestbotfor.com/best/automation](https://bestbotfor.com/best/automation), fetched October 20, 2026. The page shows \"Last reviewed Oct 15, 2026\".\n- **Our catalog and scores:** as of October 20, 2026.\n\n## How we rank (read this first)\n\n- **Match** is how well a tool matches this one job in our research. **Our rating** is a separate overall score for the tool against its category. A tool can be the strongest match for a job and still carry a middling overall rating, and we show both.\n- **Scores are research-based, not hands-on testing.** We build them from vendor pricing and product pages, documentation, public leaderboards and published reviews. We did not test these tools ourselves.\n- **Rankings are our own.** Sponsors never affect them, and payment never buys a higher rank. Sponsored placements are labeled and kept out of rankings.\n- **Links:** \"Visit\" links go through bestbotfor.com/go, which logs the click and sends you to the vendor's site. Some of those links may be affiliate links, and we may earn a commission. That never changes our picks or rankings.\n"
