    "body": "**The short answer:** when the output is a polished still image, our pick is **Midjourney** (96% match on [/best/images](https://bestbotfor.com/best/images)). There's no free plan. If the image needs readable words in it, start with **Ideogram**. For vectors, icons and consistent brand styles, choose **Recraft**. For a free tier, look at **Leonardo AI** or **Krea**.\n\n[Get your pick in 30 seconds](https://bestbotfor.com/).\n\n## Verdict by use case\n\n| If your job is... | Start with | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Art-directed images, concept art, mood | **Midjourney** | The strongest general fit when the output is a still image |\n| Fast iteration across many models | Krea | Many models in one place |\n| A full image workspace with a free tier | Leonardo AI | Free tier plus a broad toolset |\n| Images with legible text (posters, thumbnails) | Ideogram | A good default when the picture includes words |\n| Vectors, icons, consistent brand style | Recraft | Built for vectors and brand consistency |\n| Custom generation pipelines | ComfyUI | The power-user pick |\n| Image models inside your own product | FLUX | For developers |\n\n## Our pick: Midjourney\n\n**Match for this job:** 96%. **Our rating:** 3.7, #5 of 8 in Images. **Skill level:** intermediate.\n\n**Why the match and the rating differ:** match reflects output quality for still images, which is the core of this job. The overall rating also weighs price and plan limits: there's no free plan, and privacy costs more. Rivals score better on those.\n\nMidjourney is for pictures, concept art and mood. There's no free tier to plan around. It doesn't lay out a website or edit a video timeline, though its plans now include video generation.\n\n**Visit:** [Midjourney](https://bestbotfor.com/go/midjourney?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n### Pricing (verified on the vendor's own plan documentation)\n\nSource: [Midjourney docs, \"Comparing Midjourney Plans\"](https://docs.midjourney.com/hc/en-us/articles/27870484040333-Comparing-Midjourney-Plans), **checked October 20, 2026**. This is Midjourney's own help page. The logged-in plan page wasn't reachable by our checker.\n\n| Plan | Monthly | Annual (paid up front) | Fast GPU time | Relax mode |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Basic | $10 | $96 ($8/mo) | 3.3 hr/month | None |\n| Standard | $30 | $288 ($24/mo) | 15 hr/month | Unlimited images |\n| Pro | $60 | $576 ($48/mo) | 30 hr/month | Unlimited images and SD video |\n| Mega | $120 | $1,152 ($96/mo) | 60 hr/month | Unlimited images and SD video |\n\n**Also from the vendor's page:**\n- Annual plans are 20% off.\n- Extra fast GPU time is $4 per hour.\n- Stealth Mode (private images) is on Pro and Mega only.\n- Companies with more than $1,000,000 a year in gross revenue must buy Pro or Mega.\n- All plans are subscriptions that auto-renew.\n\n### Who should skip Midjourney\n\n- **You want a free plan.** Every tier is paid. Try Leonardo AI or Krea first.\n- **Your images need accurate text.** Ideogram is the better starting point.\n- **You need vector files or a repeatable brand style.** Recraft.\n- **You need privacy on a small budget.** Stealth Mode starts at $60 a month (Pro).\n- **You're a developer adding image generation to a product.** FLUX or ComfyUI.\n\n## The alternatives\n\nPrices are the labels on our live [/best/images](https://bestbotfor.com/best/images) page (October 20, 2026). They weren't re-checked on each vendor's site for this guide.\n\n**Krea: 84% match.** Free tier plus paid plans. Fast iteration with many models in one place. [Visit Krea](https://bestbotfor.com/go/krea?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n**Leonardo AI: 84% match.** A full image workspace with a free tier. [Visit Leonardo AI](https://bestbotfor.com/go/leonardo-ai?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n**Ideogram: 82% match.** A good default when the picture includes words. [Visit Ideogram](https://bestbotfor.com/go/ideogram?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n**Recraft: 82% match.** Strong for vectors, icons and consistent brand styles. [Visit Recraft](https://bestbotfor.com/go/recraft?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n**ComfyUI: 80% match.** For power users building custom generation pipelines. [Visit ComfyUI](https://bestbotfor.com/go/comfyui?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n**FLUX: 78% match.** Paid. For developers who want strong image models in their own product. [Visit FLUX](https://bestbotfor.com/go/flux?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=images)\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Is Midjourney free?** No. Plans start at $10 a month, or $8 a month billed yearly, per Midjourney's plan documentation on October 20, 2026.\n\n**Can I use Midjourney images commercially?** Midjourney's docs say subscribers can use their images under its general commercial terms, and companies over $1M in yearly gross revenue must be on Pro or Mega. Read Midjourney's Terms of Service for the details.\n\n**Did you test these tools?** No. Our scores are research-based, built from vendor pages, docs, leaderboards and published reviews.\n\n## What we checked\n\n- **Vendor pricing:** Midjourney's help page \"Comparing Midjourney Plans\" (docs.midjourney.com), read October 20, 2026 (ET). Our curl and headless-browser checks hit a security check. A text fetch of the same page succeeded.\n- **Our live ranking:** [bestbotfor.com/best/images](https://bestbotfor.com/best/images), fetched October 20, 2026. The page shows \"Last reviewed Oct 15, 2026\".\n- **Our catalog and scores:** as of October 20, 2026. Midjourney review date: October 16, 2026.\n- **Not checked for this guide:** alternative vendors' pricing pages.\n\n## How we rank (read this first)\n\n- **Match** is how well a tool matches this one job in our research. **Our rating** is a separate overall score for the tool against its category. A tool can be the strongest match for a job and still carry a middling overall rating, and we show both.\n- **Scores are research-based, not hands-on testing.** We build them from vendor pricing and product pages, documentation, public leaderboards and published reviews. We did not test these tools ourselves.\n- **Rankings are our own.** Sponsors never affect them, and payment never buys a higher rank. Sponsored placements are labeled and kept out of rankings.\n- **Links:** \"Visit\" links go through bestbotfor.com/go, which logs the click and sends you to the vendor's site. Some of those links may be affiliate links, and we may earn a commission. That never changes our picks or rankings.\n"
