    "heading": "AI voice generators compared: ElevenLabs and 6 alternatives",
    "description": "Which AI voice tool fits your job? ElevenLabs pricing checked on the vendor's site, who should skip it, and six alternatives by use case.",
    "checked": "2026-10-20",
    "body": "**The short answer:** for turning a script into natural-sounding speech, our pick is **ElevenLabs** (96% match on [/best/voice](https://bestbotfor.com/best/voice)). Speech from text is its core product, the free plan is enough to try it, and the $6 Starter plan adds a commercial license. Choose something else if you need a narration studio with a timeline (Murf), a fixed voice for corporate training (WellSaid), or a voice engine for real-time agents (Cartesia).\n\nWant the 30-second version for your own situation? [Use the picker](https://bestbotfor.com/).\n\n## Verdict by use case\n\n| If your job is... | Start with | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Voiceover for videos, ads, explainers | **ElevenLabs** | Text-to-speech is the product; a large voice library; Starter adds a commercial license |\n| Cloning your own voice | **ElevenLabs** (Starter or Creator) | Instant Voice Cloning from Starter; Professional Voice Cloning from Creator |\n| Narration for slides and training, edited on a timeline | Murf | Studio-style voiceover for scripts and presentations |\n| Consistent corporate narration across a team | WellSaid | Clean, consistent narration for training and marketing |\n| A voice for a real-time AI agent or phone bot | Cartesia | Built for real-time voice agents |\n| Lowest cost to get started | Fish Audio | Good-value voice generation with a free tier |\n| Listening to documents, not making audio for others | Speechify | Made for listening to reading material |\n| Expressive character voices for creators | Typecast | Character voices are the focus |\n\n## Our pick: ElevenLabs\n\n**Match for this job:** 96%. **Our rating:** 4.3, #1 of 6 in Voice. **Skill level:** beginner.\n\nElevenLabs is the usual pick when the job is a natural voiceover from a script. You stay in control of the script. It does not edit the picture, so you'll still need a video editor for the visuals. Alongside text-to-speech, the same plans cover speech-to-text, sound effects, voice design, dubbing and music, so one subscription can cover most audio jobs on a small project.\n\n**Visit:** [ElevenLabs](https://bestbotfor.com/go/elevenlabs?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n### Pricing (verified on the vendor's site)\n\nSource: [elevenlabs.io/pricing](https://elevenlabs.io/pricing), ElevenCreative tab, monthly billing, US locale, **checked October 20, 2026**. Prices exclude taxes.\n\n| Plan | Price | Credits per month | What it adds |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Free | $0 | 10k | Text to speech, speech to text, sound effects, voice design, music; 3 Studio projects. **No commercial license** |\n| Starter | $6/mo | 30k | Commercial license, Instant Voice Cloning, 20 Studio projects, Dubbing Studio |\n| Creator | $22/mo (first month shown at $11, a 50% promotion) | 121k | Professional Voice Cloning, extra credits |\n| Pro | $99/mo | 600k | 44.1kHz PCM output via API, 192kbps audio |\n| Scale | $299/mo | 1.8M | 3 workspace seats, team collaboration |\n| Business | $990/mo | 6M | 10 seats, low-latency TTS from about 5¢/minute |\n| Enterprise | Custom | Custom | DPA/SLA terms, HIPAA BAAs, SSO |\n\nThe vendor's comparison table estimates roughly 10 minutes of text-to-speech a month on Free, about 30 on Starter and about 121 on Creator. Usage depends on the model and settings, so treat those as the vendor's estimates. The page also offers yearly billing. We didn't record yearly prices, so check the toggle before you buy.\n\n**Pricing notes:**\n- The $11 Creator price is a first-month promotion. The regular price is $22 a month.\n- If you publish audio commercially, the Free plan isn't enough. You need Starter or above.\n\n### Who should skip ElevenLabs\n\n- **You need a narration timeline synced to slides or video.** A studio tool like Murf fits that workflow more directly.\n- **You need one locked \"house voice\" across a corporate training library with brand controls.** Look at WellSaid.\n- **You're building a low-latency voice agent and only need an API.** Cartesia is designed for that. ElevenLabs has agent products too, but compare latency and per-minute costs on both vendors' pages.\n- **You just want documents read aloud to you.** Speechify is built for listening, not producing.\n- **You want to publish commercially but pay nothing.** The free plan has no commercial license.\n\n## The alternatives\n\nPrices below are the price labels on our live [/best/voice](https://bestbotfor.com/best/voice) page (October 20, 2026), not re-checked on each vendor's site for this guide. Confirm on the vendor's page before buying.\n\n**Murf: 84% match.** Free tier plus paid plans. Studio-style voiceover for scripts and presentations. Choose it when you want to edit narration against slides. [Visit Murf](https://bestbotfor.com/go/murf?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n**WellSaid: 82% match.** Paid. Clean, consistent narration for training and marketing. Choose it for team-wide corporate voiceover. [Visit WellSaid](https://bestbotfor.com/go/wellsaid?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n**Cartesia: 80% match.** Free tier plus paid plans. Built for real-time voice agents. Choose it when latency matters more than a studio. [Visit Cartesia](https://bestbotfor.com/go/cartesia?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n**Fish Audio: 76% match.** Free tier plus paid plans. Good-value voice generation with a free tier. [Visit Fish Audio](https://bestbotfor.com/go/fish-audio?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n**Speechify: 74% match.** Made for listening to reading material. It's a reader, not a production tool. [Visit Speechify](https://bestbotfor.com/go/speechify?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n**Typecast: 74% match.** Expressive character voices for creators. [Visit Typecast](https://bestbotfor.com/go/typecast?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=voice)\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Is ElevenLabs free?** There's a free plan with 10k credits a month (about 10 minutes of text-to-speech by the vendor's estimate). It has no commercial license.\n\n**What's the cheapest way to use ElevenLabs commercially?** The Starter plan at $6 a month, per the vendor's pricing page on October 20, 2026.\n\n**Did you test these voices?** No. Our scores are research-based, built from vendor pages, documentation, leaderboards and published reviews. We didn't run hands-on tests.\n\n## What we checked\n\n- **Vendor pricing:** [elevenlabs.io/pricing](https://elevenlabs.io/pricing), rendered in a headless browser with a US locale on October 20, 2026 (ET).\n- **Our live ranking:** [bestbotfor.com/best/voice](https://bestbotfor.com/best/voice), fetched October 20, 2026. The page shows \"Last reviewed Oct 15, 2026\".\n- **Our catalog:** BestBotFor repository catalog and scores file (v2.3), as of October 20, 2026. ElevenLabs review date: October 16, 2026.\n- **Not checked for this guide:** alternative vendors' own pricing pages. Their prices come from our live page labels.\n\n## How we rank (read this first)\n\n- **Match** is how well a tool matches this one job in our research. **Our rating** is a separate overall score for the tool against its category. A tool can be the strongest match for a job and still carry a middling overall rating, and we show both.\n- **Scores are research-based, not hands-on testing.** We build them from vendor pricing and product pages, documentation, public leaderboards and published reviews. We did not test these tools ourselves.\n- **Rankings are our own.** Sponsors never affect them, and payment never buys a higher rank. Sponsored placements are labeled and kept out of rankings.\n- **Links:** \"Visit\" links go through bestbotfor.com/go, which logs the click and sends you to the vendor's site. Some of those links may be affiliate links, and we may earn a commission. That never changes our picks or rankings.\n"
