    "body": "**The short answer:** for long drafts and revision, our pick is **Claude** (88% match on [/best/writing](https://bestbotfor.com/best/writing)). It's particularly good at longer drafts and revision notes, and the free plan is a real starting point. For marketing teams that need campaigns and brand voice, look at **Jasper**. For fiction, look at **Sudowrite**. For company-wide brand rules and governance, look at **Writer**.\n\nNot sure which job you're doing? [The picker takes 30 seconds](https://bestbotfor.com/).\n\n## Verdict by use case\n\n| If your job is... | Start with | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Long drafts, rewrites, editing notes | **Claude** | Particularly good at longer drafts and revision notes |\n| Marketing campaigns in a brand voice | Jasper | Campaign and brand-voice workflows, not a general chatbot |\n| General drafting alongside other chat tasks | ChatGPT | Strong at drafts, with less structure than a marketing suite |\n| Fiction: prose, plot and revision | Sudowrite | The specialist pick for storytellers |\n| Marketing drafts on a free start | Writesonic | Marketing drafts with a free way to start |\n| Copy variants scored before you test them | Anyword | Scores variants before testing |\n| Brand rules and governance across teams | Writer | Built for companies that need governance |\n\n## Our pick: Claude\n\n**Match for this job:** 88%. **Our rating:** 4.0, #4 of 4 in Chat. **Skill level:** beginner.\n\n**Why the match and the rating differ:** the rating compares Claude with other general chat assistants across everything they do. The match score asks one question: how well does it handle writing and revising long text? That's where Claude scores well in our research.\n\nClaude is Anthropic's assistant. It handles long documents and explains things in plain language. It's still a chat product, so final edits and formatting belong in your editor or CMS. It doesn't manage campaigns, brand kits or approval workflows the way a marketing suite does.\n\n**Visit:** [Claude](https://bestbotfor.com/go/claude?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n### Pricing (verified on the vendor's site)\n\nSource: [claude.com/pricing](https://claude.com/pricing), Individual tab, **checked October 20, 2026**. Prices exclude tax.\n\n| Plan | Price | What it adds |\n|---|---|---|\n| Free | $0 | Chat on web, desktop and mobile; web search; file creation and code execution; memory; connectors; Artifacts; Projects (up to 5) |\n| Pro | $17/mo with annual billing ($200 billed up front), or $20 billed monthly | More usage, Research, Projects without the Free cap of 5, more Claude models, Claude Code, Claude in Chrome and Microsoft 365 |\n| Max | From $100/mo | 5x or 20x Pro usage, higher output limits, priority access at high-traffic times |\n\nUsage limits apply on every plan, per the vendor's page. Team and Enterprise plans are on a separate tab and weren't checked for this guide.\n\n### Who should skip Claude\n\n- **Your team runs campaigns and needs brand voice, templates and approvals in one place.** Jasper or Writer are built for that.\n- **You write fiction and want plot, character and prose tools.** Sudowrite is the specialist.\n- **You want copy variants with predicted scores.** Anyword does that. Claude doesn't score copy.\n- **You need writing that never hits a usage cap.** Every Claude plan has usage limits.\n\n## The alternatives\n\nPrices are the labels on our live [/best/writing](https://bestbotfor.com/best/writing) page (October 20, 2026). They weren't re-checked on each vendor's site for this guide.\n\n**Jasper: 86% match.** Paid. Campaign and brand-voice workflows, not a general chatbot. [Visit Jasper](https://bestbotfor.com/go/jasper?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n**ChatGPT: 84% match.** Strong at drafts, with less structure than a marketing suite. [Visit ChatGPT](https://bestbotfor.com/go/chatgpt?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n**Sudowrite: 82% match.** Paid. For storytellers who want help with prose, plot and revision. [Visit Sudowrite](https://bestbotfor.com/go/sudowrite?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n**Writesonic: 80% match.** Marketing drafts with a free way to start. [Visit Writesonic](https://bestbotfor.com/go/writesonic?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n**Anyword: 78% match.** Paid. Useful when you want copy variants scored before you test them. [Visit Anyword](https://bestbotfor.com/go/anyword?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n**Writer: 78% match.** Paid. Built for companies that need brand rules and governance across teams. [Visit Writer](https://bestbotfor.com/go/writer?utm_source=site&utm_medium=guide&utm_campaign=writing)\n\n## FAQ\n\n**Is Claude free for writing?** Yes, there's a free plan with web search, file creation and memory. Pro is $20 a month, or $17 a month billed yearly ($200 up front), per claude.com/pricing on October 20, 2026.\n\n**Claude or ChatGPT for writing?** On our live page Claude is the 88% match and ChatGPT 84%. Our research favors Claude for longer drafts and revision notes. Both are general assistants.\n\n**Did you test these tools?** No. Our scores are research-based, built from vendor pages, docs, leaderboards and published reviews.\n\n## What we checked\n\n- **Vendor pricing:** [claude.com/pricing](https://claude.com/pricing), fetched October 20, 2026 (ET).\n- **Our live ranking:** [bestbotfor.com/best/writing](https://bestbotfor.com/best/writing), fetched October 20, 2026. The page shows \"Last reviewed Oct 15, 2026\".\n- **Our catalog and scores:** as of October 20, 2026. Claude review date: October 16, 2026.\n- **Not checked for this guide:** alternative vendors' pricing pages.\n\n## How we rank (read this first)\n\n- **Match** is how well a tool matches this one job in our research. **Our rating** is a separate overall score for the tool against its category. A tool can be the strongest match for a job and still carry a middling overall rating, and we show both.\n- **Scores are research-based, not hands-on testing.** We build them from vendor pricing and product pages, documentation, public leaderboards and published reviews. We did not test these tools ourselves.\n- **Rankings are our own.** Sponsors never affect them, and payment never buys a higher rank. Sponsored placements are labeled and kept out of rankings.\n- **Links:** \"Visit\" links go through bestbotfor.com/go, which logs the click and sends you to the vendor's site. Some of those links may be affiliate links, and we may earn a commission. That never changes our picks or rankings.\n"
